Z||000003||Archie||05-13-2001||07:25 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Loki:<BR><B>Isnt there some sort of process to clean the coolant system out? A complete fluch or something?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sometimes a person gets to working on something so intently that he can't see the forest for the trees.<P>I think you are quiting the job a little bit too early. <P>I think you should give Archie a call and let him try to help you flog it.<P>Sure it could be a corrosion build up in the engine, but I doubt it, & I think Archie would doubt it too.<P>Just a few days ago another V-8 swapper was to the point of cussing because he could solve his cooling problem. In less than 3 hours another forum member gave him a suggestion that turned out to be the exact cure he had been missing all along.<P>Give Archie a call at 800-891-3608 earlt this week, I happen to know that he's leaving Thursday for Carlisle so call early in the week.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000004||V8Fiero||05-13-2001||07:46 PM||||That other swapper was me Archie. I fixed the pipe. Even flushed out the whole thing. Re Burped the whole system and added coolant/water. Tried a 180* Thermostat, even tried running without one. Still overheated. Maybe my guage isnt right. How can I check that?<P>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000005||Archie||05-13-2001||08:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by V8Fiero:<BR><B>That other swapper was me Archie. I fixed the pipe. Even flushed out the whole thing. Re Burped the whole system and added coolant/water. Tried a 180* Thermostat, even tried running without one. Still overheated. Maybe my guage isnt right. How can I check that?<P>Scott</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sorry about the confusion.... this is why I recommended that you call me. It would take me 6 hours of typing to cover all the suggestions, questions & responses and follow-up questions. It would only take 15 minutes to go thru it on the phone. If you've been working on it this long and just now found the bent cooling pipe.... then I wonder how many other items you've overlooked or not considered.<P>For example in your statement above you stated "Still overheated" then in the next line you ask/state that it could be your temp gage. My first Question would be "did the car actually overheat (like in boil over) or are you calling a high temp. reading Overheating?"<P>I have a bunch more questions before I can help you sort it out. To be honest with you, I don't feel like typing all those questions out.<P>The best way to check your original Fiero temp gage is to hook up an aftermarket gage to dblcheck against it.<P>Archie||||reg||1
